@startuml

title Project Workflow - Role Separation

|Product Owner|
start
:Create New Project;
:Add Scrum Master to Project;
:Create Epics;
:Create User Stories;
:Assign Epic/Story to Scrum Master;
note right
  PO focuses on WHAT needs to be done
  and WHY (business value)
end note
:Prioritize Backlog;

|Scrum Master|
:Receive Assigned Epics/Stories;
:Add Developers to Team;
:Add Testers to Team;
:Define Detailed Acceptance Criteria;
note right
  SM focuses on HOW it will be done
  and WHO will do it
end note
:Estimate Story Points;
:Create Sprint;
:Add Stories to Sprint;
:Decompose Stories into Tasks;
:Assign Tasks to Team Members;
:Configure Kanban Board;
:Set Tester-Only Columns;
note right
  Mark "Testing", "QA Review", "Done" 
  as testerOnly = true
end note

|Developer|
:Pick Assigned Task;
:Move Task to "In Progress";
:Implement Feature;
:Move Task to "Code Review";
note right
  Developer CANNOT move to
  tester-only columns
end note
:Wait for Tester;

|Tester|
:Review Code;
if (Code Review Passed?) then (yes)
  :Move Task to "Testing" (testerOnly);
  note right
    Only Tester can move here
    because testerOnly = true
  end note
  :Execute Test Cases;
  :Validate Acceptance Criteria;
  if (All Tests Passed?) then (yes)
    :Move Task to "Done" (testerOnly);
    note right
      Only Tester can mark as done
    end note
  else (no)
    :Report Bug;
    |Developer|
    :Move Task to "In Progress";
    :Fix Bug;
    :Move to "Code Review";
    |Tester|
    :Re-test;
  endif
else (no)
  |Developer|
  :Move Task to "In Progress";
  :Fix Code Issues;
  |Tester|
endif

|Scrum Master|
:Monitor Sprint Progress;
:Track Burndown;
:Remove Impediments;

if (Sprint Ended?) then (yes)
  :Close Sprint;
  |Product Owner|
  :Review Completed Work;
  :Accept/Reject Features;
  :View Sprint Report;
  :Plan Next Sprint;
  stop
else (no)
  |Developer|
  :Continue Development;
endif

@enduml
